        <h2 class="mh-about-origin-headline">An Enterprise Perspective, Built Over Two Decades</h2>
        <p>Most platforms start with a feature idea. MedhaIQ started with a pattern observed over 25 years of leading global consulting practices, enterprise transformations, and talent initiatives across North America, EMEA, and APAC.</p>
        <p>Technical skill opens the door—but the ability to structure an argument, read a room, and communicate under pressure decides how far someone walks through it. Yet across every tier of the enterprise, three systemic realities persist:</p>
      </div>

      <ul class="mh-about-gaps">
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">01</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">Feedback arrives too late.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">Professionals rarely receive actionable input until after the opportunity has passed.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">02</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">The first real attempt happens at the highest stakes.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">Practice occurs during the actual interview, pitch, or board review.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="mh-about-gap">
          <span class="mh-about-gap-mark">03</span>
          <div>
            <div class="mh-about-gap-title">Evaluation is often subjective.</div>
            <p class="mh-about-gap-text">Capability is frequently judged on impression rather than structured, evidence-based metrics.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

